{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1792711544596,"sessionID":"ses_e9a22f168ffeMitJv1wz5wxyzc","part":{"id":"prt_165ee0e47001NZoy9t9B77tMep","sessionID":"ses_e9a22f168ffeMitJv1wz5wxyzc","messageID":"msg_165ee0a840016tgMy9PYT435mv","type":"reasoning","text":"So 20/11/2026 (Friday), 21/11 (Saturday), 22/11 (Sunday), 23/11 (Monday) — is_bday(2026-11-20) must be False. Let me check: 20/11/2026 is a Friday. Why is it not a business day? Let me check... 20/11/2026 is actually the \"Dia Nacional de Zumbi e da Consciência Negra (Lei 14.759/2023)\"! It's in the calendar table as 20/11/2026 (sex). So 20/11 IS a holiday/business closure. That's why next_business_after(19/11) skips 20/11 (Fri holiday) and lands on 23/11 (Mon).\n\nWait, but that affects the citation timeline. The citation was published 19/11 (Thu), count starts 20/11 → but 20/11 is a holiday (Zumbi/Zumbi day, sem prazo per... actually not listed as sem prazo). Let me verify: the calendar lists \"20/11/2026 (sex) | Dia Nacional de Zumbi e da Consciência Negra (Lei 14.759/2023)\". 20/11/2026 is a Friday. So it is a holiday.\n\nSo inicio contagem for citação = 23/11/2026 (Monday), and the count goes:\n24/11(Fri), 30/11(Mon), 1/12...11/12(Fri), 14/12(Mon) → vencimento 14/12/2026 (Mon).\n\nThe citação (19/11→contação) does NOT cross the recess (recess starts 20/12), so recess not involved there.\n\nNow the sentença recuso (apelação) DOES cross recess. inicio = 21/12 (first bday after 10/12/2026 Thu, skipping 20/12 recess start, 22-25 weekend/Natal, 27-31 weekend/no-exp). So 21/12/2026 (Thu). Count 15 days:\n14/12(Mon),15,16,17,18/12, [recess 20/12..20/01 skip], 21/01? wait 21/01 is first bday after recess. 21/01(Thu),22/01(Fri),25/01(Mon, but São Paulo capital holiday doesn't apply in Campinas per calendar),26,27,28,29/01, 31/01? no wait need to recount.\n\nFrom calc.py output: inicio contagem Fri 11/12? That's WRONG. Let me recheck: \"inicio contagem (art. 224o3 / 231VII): Monday 23/11/2026\" for citação — wait no, that's the citação. Let me re-read calc.py output:\n\nCITACAO 19/11: publicacao Thu 19/11, inicio contagem Mon 23/11. ✓ (because 20/11 is Zumbi holiday)\ncount: 24/11,30/11,01/12...11/12,14/12 → VENCIMENTO Mon 14/12/2026. ✓\n\nSENTENCA 10/12: publicacao Thu 10/12, inicio contagem... it printed \"Friday 11/12/2026\". That's WRONG — should be 21/12. Wait, let me recompute. first_business_after(Thu 10/12/2026): 11/12 is Friday (bday) → 21/12. But calc.py says inicio contagem Fri 11/12/2026!\n\nThat means in calc.py, 10/12 was treated as... wait, is_bday(10/12/2026)? 10/12 is \"N. Sra. Aparecida\" — the calendar lists \"12/10/2026 (seg) | N. Sra. Aparecida\". But 12/10/2026 is a Monday? The calendar says (seg)=Monday. But actually 12/10/2026 is a Tuesday! Hmm, the calendar may have errors, but per the calendar table we must follow it. 12/10 is not 10/12 though. 10/12/2026 is December 10. The calendar lists \"12/12/... none\". 10/12 = Dec 10 = Thursday per my weekday. So is_bday(10/12/2026)=True, first_business_after = 11/12 (Fri). \n\nSo calc.py's sentença inicio contagem = Fri 11/12/2026. That's DIFFERENT from my manual trace where I assumed 21/12. Let me look at calc.py output again:\n\n\"=== SENTENCA -> recurso ===\n  disponibilidade: Thursday 10/12/2026\n  publicacao: Thursday 10/12/2026\n  inicio contagem: Friday 11/12/2026\n    Monday 14/12/2026\n    ...\n    Tuesday 22/01/2027\n    Monday 25/01/2027\n    ...\nWednesday 03/02/2027\"\n\nWait, it skipped from 18/12 to ... let me see the sequence. The count: 11/12 is inicio, first counted 14/12(Mon),15,16,17,18/12 → that's 5 days. Then it would continue 21/12 → BUT recess starts 20/12! So 21/12 is INSIDE recess until 20/01. So from 18/12 next counted: skip to after recess. 21/12..20/01 all recess → none count. Next bday 21/01/2027.\n\nWait, but calc.py inicio contagem says Fri 11/12/2026 and it counted. Let me re-examine. Actually the calc.py output I need to re-read. It said:\n\n\"inicio contagem (art. 224o3 / 231VII): Friday 11/12/2026\"\nthen counted: Mon 14/12, Tue 15, Wed 16, Thu 17, Fri 18, then Thursday 21/01, Friday 22/01, Monday 25/01...\n\nSo the jump 18/12 → 21/01 (skipping recess). Yes! So sentença recuso vencimento = Wed 03/02/2027.\n\nThat matches my earlier calc.py run. Good. And embargos 5 dias uteis from 11/12: 14,15,16,17,18/12 → Fri 18/12/2026. ✓\n\nSo final answers:\n- contestação: venc 14/12/2026 (Mon)\n- embargos de declaração: venc 18/12/2026 (Fri)\n- apelação: venc 03/02/2027 (Wed)\n\nNow the interpretation issue: A) count starts next bday after pub → 15 days → 14/12. B) 231VII says start = pub date itself, count inclusive → different (13/12). I'll go with A (start = next bday, art. 224 §3º as the governing rule for count commencement), but note the tension with 231VII.\n\nNow the double-prazo question: The client believes double prazo (art. 229 caput: 2 réus, different law firms). BUT Art. 229 §2º says the doubling does NOT apply to \"processos em autos eletrônicos\". This is an e-SAJ electronic process, so the double-prazo does NOT apply. This is the key issue — the client's belief is likely WRONG. And crucially, whether double applies affects nothing for the contestação date (15 days).\n","metadata":{"reasoningField":"reasoning"},"time":{"start":1792711462471,"end":1792711544596}}}
