nHmm, 28/11 is Saturday (already skipped by weekend). So skipping 28/11 explicitly vs. as weekend = NO DIFFERENCE — it's already a weekend! So the prior work's claim to skip 28/11 had no actual effect on the count, because 28/11 is a Saturday.\n\nBut the prior work did NOT skip 08/12 (treating it 08/12 as a normal day, using it as day 7 in the mislabeled table). THAT's the real error. So prior contestação (14/12) is off by one — should be 15/12.\n\nLet me verify: prior day 7 = 08/12. In correct counting, 08/12 is a holiday (skip), so:\n- Prior: ...5=30(11),6=01(12),7=08(12)? No wait, prior skipped 28/11 and had 6=01/12, then 7=08/12? That skips 02,03,04/12 too. The prior table is just a mess with wrong ordering.\n\nI'll stop trying to parse the prior table. Let me just compute cleanly with a script and trust it. The script uses correct business-day rules: weekends + holidays {20/11, 08/12, 24/12, 25/12, 31/12, 01/01} + recess {20/12-20/01}.\n\nLet me now also recompute the recurso cleanly with correct weekdays to resolve 02 vs 03 Feb.\n\nRecurso (15 business days), início = 11/12 (Fri) excluded:\n- 11/12 Fri = início (excluded)\n- 12/12 Sat, 13/12 Sun\n- 14/12 Mon = day 1\n- 15/12 Tue = day 2\n- 16/12 Wed = day 3\n- 17/12 Thu = day 4\n- 18/12 Fri = day 5\n- 19/12 Sat (skip)\n- 20/12 recess begins\n- recess through 20/01/2027\n- 21/01/2027: what weekday? 18/12 Thu→ but with recess, resume. 20/01 is last recess day (Sunday). 21/01 = Monday (since 01/01 Fri, 01/01+20days... let me just: 25/01 Monday as computed earlier, so 21/01 = Thu? No. Let me compute: 01/01/2027 = Friday. +20 days = 21/01. 20 days = 2 weeks + 6 days. Friday + 6 = Thursday. So 21/01 = Thursday. Hmm, but that doesn't match 25/01=Monday (Thursday+4=Monday ✓). Good, 21/01 = Thursday.\n\nWait, but recess is 20/12/2026 to 20/01/2027. So day counting resumes on the FIRST business day after recess. First business day after 20/01: 21/01 (Thu) — business day. \n\nContinue recurso count:\n- 21/01 Thu = day 6\n- 22/01 Fri = day 7\n- 23/01 Sat, 24/01 Sun (skip)\n- 25/01 Mon = day 8 (N.Paulo is capital-only, so business in Campinas)\n- 26/01 Tue = day 9\n- 27/01 Wed = day 10\n- 28/01 Thu = day 11\n- 29/01 Fri = day 12\n- 30/01 Sat, 31/01 Sun (skip)\n- 01/02 Mon = day 13\n- 02/02 Tue = day 14\n- 03/02 Wed = day 15 → vencimento!\n\nSo recurso vencimento = **03/02/2027 (Wednesday)**. Confirmed 03/02.\n\nWhere did 02/02 come from? If someone did NOT skip a business day, or counted day 1 = 11/12 (the inicio) instead of excluding it → then every day shifts by 1, giving 02/02. Or if 25/01 were treated as holiday. So 03/02 is correct under proper art. 224 (exclude start day).\n\nSo the correct answer: recurso/simple contestação vencimento = 03/02/2027; contestação = 15/12/2026.\n\nNow let me reconsider the contestação once more with the corrected rule, being 100% sure.\n\nAlso I want to double-check: is inicio_contagem = 23/11 or is it possible the \"publicação\" and \"inicio\" should be handled differently? Let me re-examine art. 224 §4 vs §3 and Lei 11419 §4.\n\n- Lei 11.419 §3º: publicação = 1º útil seguinte à disponibilidade.\n- Lei 11.419 §4º: prazo inicia no 1º útil seguinte à data da publicação.\n- CPC 224 §2º: publicação = 1º útil seguinte à disponibilidade (same).\n- CPC 224 §3º: contagem inicia no 1º útil seguinte à publicação.\n\nPublicação = 19/11 (since 19/11 is business day, publicação = 19/11). Início da contagem = 1º útil seguinte à publicação (19/11) = 23/11 (skip 20/11 Zumbi, 21-22 weekend). So início = 23/11/2026. Correct — this fixes the on-disk error (20/11).\n\nAnd dia comeco (23/11) is excluded per art. 224. So day 1 = 24/11. Good. This matches my contestação count.\n\nNow, let me verify all with the script and also compute the DOBRO values:\n- Contestação 30 dias úteis (dobro): count 30 business days from 24/11.\n- Recurso 30 dias úteis (dobro): count 30 business days from 11/12... but recurso dobros through recess again.\n\nBut per art. 229 §2º, doubling in autos eletrônicos is questionable. I'll present simple as the definitive and doubling as sensitivity.\n\nWait, actually I should reconsider whether dobro changes the contestação vencimento. 30 business days from day 1 (24/11):\nLet me continue from contestação: day 15 = 15/12/202. Beyond recess. Let me count to 30:\n16=16(12),17=17(12),18=18(12),[19Sat,20RCESS],...21/01=19? \n\nWait I need to be careful. Let me recount from day 15:\n14=14/12(Mon),15=15/12(Tue),16=16/12(Wed),17=17/12(Thu),18=18/12(Fri),19/12=Sat skip,20/12 recess start, recess 20/12-20/01...\nAfter recess: 21/01(Thu)=19,22/01(Fri)=20,23,24 weekend,25/01(Mon)=21,26/01=22,27/01=23,28/01=24,29/01=25,30,31 weekend,01/02=26,02/02=27,03/02=28,[04/02 Sat? no]. \n\nWait, 03/02 = day 28. Continue: 04/02 (Sun)? Let me get weekdays. 01/02 Mon(26),02/02 Tue(27),03/02 Wed(28),04/02 Thu(29),05/02 Fri(30). So contestação 30-day = 05/02/2027 (Friday), not 04/02.\n\nWait let me recompute 25/01 weekday. 01/01/2027 = Friday (calendar says 01/01/2027 (sex)). +24 days = 25/01. 24 days = 3 weeks + 3 days. Friday + 3 = Monday. So 25/01 = Monday. ✓. So my count continues: after recess 21/01 is Thursday? 25/01 = Monday → 21/01 = Thursday (Monday - 4 = Thursday). ✓.\n\nSo day 19 = 21/01 (Thu), day 20 = 22/01 (Fri), 23/01 Sat, 24/01 Sun skip, day 21 = 25/01 (Mon), 22=26/01, 23=27/01, 24=28/01, 25=29/01, 30/01 Sat, 31/01 Sun skip, day 26 = 01/02 (Mon), 27=02/02, 28=03/02, 29=04/02, 30=05/02. So contestação 30-day vence **05/02/2027**.\n\nPrior work said 04/02 for dobro. Off by one due to the same 08/12 vs 28/11 error. Correct = 05/02/2027.\n\nHmm wait, let me double check 18/12 through recess. day 18 = 18/12 (Fri). Then 19/12 (Sat) skip, 20/12 recess. Good.\n\nRecurso 30-day: start 11/12 excluded, day1=14/12. Through recess, day 15 = 03/02 (computed earlier). Continue to 30:\n16=04/02(Thu),17=05/02(Fri),06/02(Sat),07/02(Sun),08/02/2027(Carnaval - HOLIDAY!), 09/02(Carnaval - holiday),10/02(Mon)=...\n\nWait! 08/02 and 09/02/2027 are Carnaval holidays (calendar says \"08/02/2027 (seg) | Carnaval\" and \"09/02/2027 (ter) | Carnaval\")! So they're holidays, skip. But does the 30-day recurso reach them? day 15=03/02, 16=04/02, 17=05/02, [06,07 weekend], 08/02 Carnaval skip, 09/02 Carnaval skip, 10/02 Mon = day 18, 19/02, 20/02, 21/02, 22/02... \n\nLet me count: day 18=10/02, 19=11/02, 20=12/02, 21=13/02(Fri), [14,15 wknd], 16=16/02, 17=17/02, 18=18/02, 19=19/02, 20=20/02, ... 30 days:\nday15=03/02,16=04/02,17=05/02,18=10/02,19=11/02,20=12/02,21=13/02,22=16/02,23=17/02,24=18/02,25=19/02,26=20/02,27=23/02,28=24/02,29=25/02,30=26/02.\n\nSo recurso 30-day = 26/02/2027 (roughly). This is far into the future and the client only cares about the simple prazo dates really. But I'll include doubling as sensitivity. Actually, since art. 229 §2º likely excludes doubling in electronico autos, and the recurso vencimento is the SAME whether doubled or not (because—hmm, actually the recess and holidays differ, so doubling DOES change recurso vencimento: 15-day=03/02, 30-day=26/02).\n\nWait — the prior work claimed \"dobro não altera data de vencimento dos recursos\" — but that's only true if recess/holidays don't fall in the window. Here 08/02 Carnaval DOES fall in the 30-day window, so doubling DOES change the resource date. Hmm, but actually let me reconsider. The prior work's logic was that recurso is the same. Let me recompute: 15-day recurso = 03/02/2027 (Wed). 30-day recurso = 26/02/2027. These ARE different (because Carnaval 08-09/02 falls in the second half of the 30-day period). So doubling DOES affect the resource date.\n\nBut is doubling even applicable? Per art. 229 §2º, no (autos eletrônicos). So the resource vence 03/02/2027 (simple) is the defensible number. Doubling is speculative.\n\nHmm, but actually the prior work's statement about dobro not affecting recurso might be based on a different recess interpretation. Let me reconsider whether recess suspends the recurso at all, or whether... no,