{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1792715110630,"sessionID":"ses_e9a22f168ffeMitJv1wz5wxyzc","part":{"id":"prt_1661ef7230013ANKaIuzhHcD5b","sessionID":"ses_e9a22f168ffeMitJv1wz5wxyzc","messageID":"msg_1661eef67001A5uaigTdSj3hDW","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have the full picture. Let me carefully cross-check the facts against the library:\n\n**IMPORTANT DISCOVERY:** The old `memoria.md` cites contestação as **\"15 dias úteis (art. 335, III)\"** but the lib's `cpc_prazos_recursais.md` shows **Art. 335** reads: \"O réu poderá oferecer contestação... no prazo de **15 (quinze) dias**, cujo termo inicial será a data: ... III – prevista no art. 231...\" \n\nSo contestação IS art. 335 III, 15 dias. The old file was RIGHT about art. 335, III. Wait, the summary said the old file cited contestação as art. 335 III but the library says art. 336 §1º. Let me re-read. Actually the library `cpc_prazos_recursais.md` says \"**Art. 335.** O réu poderá oferecer contestação, por petição, no prazo de **15 (quinze) dias**, cujo termo inicial será a data: ... III – prevista no art. 231\". So art. 335, III is correct (15 dias). Good — my summary note was wrong; the library uses art. 335, III. The memoria.md correctly used art. 335 III. \n\nNow let me verify all the citations used against what's actually in the library index (only those may be cited):\n\nLibrary index files:\n- `calendario_forense_campinas.md` — calendar\n- `cpc_prazos.md` — arts. 219, 220, 224, 229, 231\n- `cpc_prazos_recursais.md` — CPC arts. 335, 1.003 §5º, 1.023 (note: it mentions art. 1.026 inline but the citation line says \"335, 1.003 §5º, 1.023\"; 1.026 appears as text)\n- `lei11419_art4.md` — Lei 11.419/2006, art. 4º §§3º e 4º\n\nNow let me check the old memoria.md citations:\n1. **art. 219** — in cpc_prazos.md ✓ (dias úteis)\n2. **art. 224 §1/§2/§3** — in cpc_prazos.md ✓\n3. **art. 231 VII** — in cpc_prazos.md ✓\n4. **art. 220** — in cpc_prazos.md ✓ (recesso)\n5. **art. 335 III** — in cpc_prazos_recursais.md ✓ (contestação, 15 dias)... old memoria said \"15 dias\" — but wait, the old memoria.md section 2 table said \"Recursos em geral (apelação) = 15 dias úteis | **art. 1.003, §5º**\" and contestação referenced art. 335 III in section 3. Actually let me check. Old file section 3 said \"Prazo: 15 dias úteis (art. 335, III).\" ✓ Good.\n6. **art. 1.023** (embargos 5 dias) — in cpc_prazos_recursais.md ✓\n7. **art. 1.026** (embargos interrompe recurso) — this appears in the body text of cpc_prazos_recursais.md: \"§… a oposição de embargos **interrompe** o prazo para a interposição de recurso (art. 1.026).\" So although the citation line lists \"335, 1.003 §5º, 1.023\", the article 1.026 is present in the file text. It's citable via the file even though not in the header citation. This is fine since it's within a library file.\n8. **art. 1.003 §5º** (recursos 15 dias) — in cpc_prazos_recursais.md ✓\n9. **art. 229 caput/§1/§2** (dobro) — in cpc_prazos.md ✓\n10. **art. 4º §3º** (Lei 11.419/2006) — in lei11419_art4.md ✓\n11. **Lei 14.759/2023** (Zumbi) — referenced in library citation of both cpc... no, calendar file citation \"Lei 14.759/2023\" ✓\n\nWait — the old file also cited **art. 335, III** — hmm actually wait. Let me reconsider something. The old memoria said in the contestação section \"15 dias úteis (art. 335, III)\" — but the actual CPC article for contestação is **336, §1º** in the real CPC. However, the LIBRARY is the authority and the library file `cpc_prazos_recursais.md` explicitly gives **Art. 335** for contestação (\"O réu poderá oferecer contestação... no prazo de 15 dias... III – prevista no art. 231\"). So per the library, contestação = art. 335, III. I must use what the library says, not real-world CPC. So **art. 335, III is correct** per the library. Good.\n\nSo the old memoria was actually mostly correct on citations. The main issues are:\n1. **Corrupted encoding** (malformed UTF-8 / mojibake) — MUST fix.\n2. **Wrong inicio_contagem for contestação**: old file says \"20/11/2026\"; the authoritative calc5.py says **23/11/2026** (because 20/11 is Zumbi → protraito to 23/11). This is the key legal nuance. The old file had it wrong.\n\n   Wait — actually let me reconsider this very carefully, because it's the crux. Let me think about the legal logic of both the old file and calc5.\n\n   **The old memoria approach:**\n   - Publicação = disponibilidade day (19/11) since 19/11 is a business day.\n   - Início da contagem = 1º útil seguinte = 20/11 (skipping nothing since 20/11 exists as a business day... but wait, 20/11 is Zumbi per calendar = \"Dia Nacional de Zumbi\"). The old file didn't account for Zumbi.\n   - Then counted 15 business days starting 20/11 as day 0 (excluded), so first business day counted = 23/11.\n   - Result: vencimento 14/12/2026 (also a Monday, coincidentally same as calc5).\n\n   Wait, both arrive at 14/12/2026 for contestação vencimento! Because the \"início\" (20/11 vs 23/11) is just the starting point, and the number of business days counted differs... let me check.\n\n   Old file counted (section 3): day 1 = 24/11... day 15 = 14/12. It excluded 20/11 as dia do começo.\n   calc5 counted: inicio_contagem=23/11 (Mon), day 1 = 24/11 ... day 15 = 14/12. Also excludes 23/11 as dia do começo.\n\n   Hmm, so both get 14/12 for the vencimento! Because:\n   - Old: excludes 20/11, 21-22 weekend, then counts 23/11 (Mon), 24... wait no. Old file started counting at 24/11 as day 1. Let me re-read old file section 3.\n\n   Old file section 3:\n   ```\n   1 | 24/11 | 6 | 01/12/26 | 11 | 07/12\n   2 | 25/11 | 7 | 08/12 | 12 | 09/12\n   3 | 26/11 | 8 | 09/12 | 13 | 10/12   ← note \"09/12\" duplicated typo\n   4 | 27/11 | 9 | 10/12 | 14 | 11/12\n   5 | 30/11 | 10 | 11/12 | 15 | 14/12/2026\n   ```\n   So old counted day1=24/11,...,day15=14/12. It EXCLUDED 20/11,21,22 (weekend+Zumbi... actually it said \"Pula-se 21–22/11 (sábado/domingo), 28/11\"). It didn't mention 20/11 Zumbi. It treated 20/11 as dia do começo (excluded via art.224§1 \"excluindo o dia do começo\"), not as a holiday. So it just didn't count 20/11 because it's the start day.\n\n   calc5: inicio_contagem = 23/11 (because 20/11 Zumbi protraita o início ao 23/11). Then counts 15 business days AFTER 23/11: day1=24/11,...,day15=14/12.\n\n   So the difference between the two is purely the interpretation of what \"inicio_contagem\" is (20/11 vs 23/11). Both yield vencimento 14/12. Interesting. The difference matters because with the \"inicio_contagem=23/11\" interpretation, you exclude 23/11 (already a holiday-free Monday) and count 15 days after. With \"inicio_contagem=20/11\" interpretation (old file), you exclude 20/11 and count 15 business days after — but wait, that would give day1=23/11... no.\n\n   Hmm, actually I need to be careful. Let me re-examine. If inicio=20/11 is the \"dia do começo\" and you EXCLUDE it per art 224, and count 15 business days after it, ignoring that 20/11 is a holiday:\n   - After 20/11: next business day (Mon 23/11) = day 1... \n   \n   Old file had day 1 = 24/11, NOT 23/11! So the old file actually EXCLUDED both 20/11 AND 23/11. That's inconsistent — it excluded 23/11 as if it were a non-business day but then... actually the old file section 3 skipped from \"publicação inicio 20/11\" and day1=24/11, effectively skipping 23/11. That seems buggy. But it still landed on 14/12 because... let me recount.\n\n   Actually let me carefully trace both to see if they really both give 14/12.\n\n   **calc5 (authoritative):**\n   - inicio_contagem = 23/11/2026.\n   - Count 15 business days AFTER 23/11 (excluding 23/11 itself): \n     1=24/11(Tue), 2=25/11, 3=26/11, 4=27/11, 5=30/11(Mon), 6=01/12, 7=02/12, 8=03/12, 9=04/12, 10=07/12(Mon), 11=08/12, 12=09/12, 13=10/12, 14=11/12, 15=14/12(Mon).\n   - vencimento = **14/12/2026**. ✓ (note 08/12 is \"N.Sra da Conceição\" municipal ferial in Campinas per calendar = 08/12/2026 (ter) N. Sra. da Conceição — feriado municipal! But 08/12/2026 is a Tuesday. Wait,